 Oh, come on.  There's lots more overpreparation he COULD have done.

Just off the top of my head...

A dedicated over-preparer would have taken the silver saber back down
to +5 and re-blessed-enchanted it to +7.  Also, doing the same with
Excalibur would provide an excellent spare in case any unfortunate
thing should happen to Grayswandir.  (I've had things happen to
deprive me of my primary weapon on the way back up from the Sanctum.
It happens.)  The daggers could also have been usefully enchanted
to +7 -- sometimes you just want to kill something without stepping
into melee range, you know?  Also, a blessed +7 unicorn horn in main
inventory and a backup blessed +7 unicorn horn in the bag of holding
(in case the main one gets cursed in combat) wouldn't hurt either.

Since the cloak of MR was the only source of MR, the enchantment on
the robe is effectively meaningless, as you're never going to wear it
in anything resembling a potential combat situation, but the speed
boots and gloves could have usefully been brought up to +5.  The
gloves, being the mundane variety, could have been enchanted to +6
or maybe even higher, given sufficient stock of magic markers.

Only eight potions of holy water in the bag?  I know potions are
heavy, but you can blow through eight holy water pretty quick if
you run into a swarm of things that curse stuff, especially when
you're not carrying any blessed scrolls of remove curse.  Far more
likely than needing all twenty K-rats.

Luck could have been much higher, as well.

(Note:  I'm not criticizing the OP.  Manifestly, the extant level
of overpreparation was adequate, given that the character ascended.
I'm just saying, much more overpreparation would've been possible.)


